# P175 -- WebAssembly (wasm32_wasi).
#
# DELIBERATELY THE SAME FILE LIST AS linux_x86_64.  The wasm demo profile removes C++ FEATURES
# (sockets, termios, NCG); it does not remove Scheme library files, and keeping the two lists
# identical is what makes "does it behave like the Linux build?" a meaningful question -- a
# divergence here would show up as a conform failure that is really a missing file.
#
# tools/llip-*.scm ARE staged even though LL_NETWORK=0 leaves this build with no
# open-tcp-server-port.  They are not loaded at startup; staging them keeps the FS identical and
# lets the demo SHOW the protocol source.  Loading one will fail at the first socket call, which
# is the correct and visible outcome, not a silent one.
#
# NOTHING IN HERE MAY PRODUCE A TIMING NUMBER FOR PUBLICATION.  A wasm host JITs our interpreter
# and a browser tab throttles it; P175 is explicit that this is a LANGUAGE demo.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/linux.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/I2C.scm
